 <h2>mobilityDCAT-AP Serialisation Files</h2>
 
-<p>Serialisation files the allow for IT implementations of mobilityDCAT-AP are available as RDF/XML, Turtle, and JSON-LD syntaxes at <a href="https://github.com/mobilityDCAT-AP/mobilityDCAT-AP/tree/gh-pages/releases">this Github subfolder</a>.</p>
+<p>To support IT implementations of the mobilityDCAT-AP specification, machine-readable serialisations of the specification are provided in three standard RDF syntaxes. RDF/XML is the original XML-based syntax for RDF, widely supported by older tools and libraries. Turtle offers a more compact, human-readable format often preferred for manual inspection or editing. JSON-LD expresses RDF as JSON, integrating naturally with web applications and modern JavaScript/API-based tooling. Together, these formats give developers a ready-to-use, machine-readable version of the specification, so they can work directly with the data model in their applications rather than encoding it by hand.
+
+The serialisation files are available in the releases subfolder of the <a href="https://github.com/mobilityDCAT-AP/mobilityDCAT-AP/tree/gh-pages/releases">mobilityDCAT-AP GitHub repository</a>.</p>
 
